AI models (downloaded by the app, not part of it)

- Whisper-Large-V3-Turbo by OpenAI, as quantized (w8a16) and compiled for Snapdragon NPUs by Qualcomm AI Hub
  (Whisper-Large-V3-Turbo-Quantized, https://huggingface.co/qualcomm/Whisper-Large-V3-Turbo-Quantized, release
  v0.65.0, precompiled_qnn_onnx), Apache License 2.0 per its model card (its License section links
  https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/v4.42.3/LICENSE). The source checkpoint,
  openai/whisper-large-v3-turbo (https://huggingface.co/openai/whisper-large-v3-turbo), is MIT License per its model
  card, Copyright (c) OpenAI. A chip given AI Hub's float build instead
  (https://huggingface.co/qualcomm/Whisper-Large-V3-Turbo, Apache License 2.0 per its model card) downloads that one;
  none does at present.
- UVR-MDX-NET-Voc_FT by the Ultimate Vocal Remover team (Anjok07, aufr33), MIT License, with credit to UVR and
  its developers, as UVR's README asks of third-party application developers
  (https://github.com/Anjok07/ultimatevocalremovergui). Architecture: KUIELab MDX-Net. Downloaded from
  https://github.com/TRvlvr/model_repo/releases/tag/all_public_uvr_models. The licence comes from UVR's README
  note, not from a licence file next to the weights; training data are not documented.
- wav2vec2-base-960h by Facebook AI (https://huggingface.co/facebook/wav2vec2-base-960h),
  Apache License 2.0, as exported to ONNX and quantized to 4 bits (onnx/model_q4.onnx) by Xenova
  (https://huggingface.co/Xenova/wav2vec2-base-960h).

